<title>UK: Vickers up on disposal news, Hoare positive.</title>
<headline>Vickers up on disposal news, Hoare positive.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British engineering group Vickers Plc firmed on Friday after the company announced it was in talks to sell its S&amp;W Medico Teknik unit to Sweden's Artema Medical AB.</p>
<p>ABN AMRO Hoare Govett analyst Sandy Morris said the news was positive for the company and he was restating his &quot;buy&quot; recommendation on the stock.</p>
<p>&quot;S&amp;W has been a problem child for some time and it is positive news that they may have grasped the nettle and may achieve a strategic solution,&quot; Morris said.</p>
<p>The shares were seven pence firmer at 216 by 1123 GMT.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Marshall, London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
</text>
